    {
      "bbox": [
        314,
        264,
        1473,
        718
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "(a) The Committee shall be appointed by the Mayor and shall consist of seven members, including a chair, each residing or having a principal place of business in the City of New York. The members may, in their discretion, designate adjunct members who shall function under section four as voting members with regard to appointments and reappointments to specific commissions, boards or other public bodies. Adjunct members, if so designated, shall be professionals or knowledgeable persons of high standing with expertise appropriate for enabling the Committee to make a reasoned, informed and impartial evaluation of candidates for the offices referred to in section two. If so designated, there shall be between two and four adjunct members for each commission, board or other public body for which candidates are evaluated according to the determination of the members.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.2832,
          "min": -1.4382
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
